            <ArticleTitle>Aneurysm of left ventricle and left coronary artery after non-penetrating chest trauma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>495-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 17 year old boy who sustained blunt chest trauma to his chest developed a proximal left anterior descending coronary artery aneurysm and an aneurysm of the left ventricle. He underwent left ventricular aneurysmectomy and was discharged to outpatient follow up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
